e cmd-package functions that no longer exist.\n\nThe task says: \"随函数迁移同步改写 `internal/cmd/{plan,doing,easy}_test.go` 中引用已迁函数的断言（executePlanWorkflow/executeDoingWorkflow/loadTasksFromPlan 等）；另改写 `tools_test.go`（`runDoingDryRun` 引用）与 `dryrun_integration_test.go`（`runPlanDryRun` 引用）\".\n\nSo I need to rewrite those tests to reference handler package functions (or remove/move them).\n\nLet me think about what tests to keep in cmd and what to move to handler.\n\nThe cleanest approach:\n- Move the tests for migrated functions to `internal/handler/` package tests. But that's a lot of work. Alternatively, rewrite the cmd tests to call handler functions.\n\nLet me list the references that break:\n\nplan_test.go:\n- `generateJobID()` — deleted; TestGenerateJobID must be removed (or rewritten). Since we delete generateJobID, remove TestGenerateJobID.\n- `reEnterPlanWorkflow(\"job_999\", ...)` — now `handler.ReEnterPlan`\n- `executePlanWorkflow(\"test requirement\")` — now `handler.Plan`\n\ndoing_test.go:\n- `extractTaskNumber` — now in handler (unexported). If I want to test it, I'd need to export or move test to handler package. The test6 structural check only requires 9 exported functions. extractTaskNumber can stay unexported in handler. But the doing_test.go test `TestExtractTaskNumber` references it. I need to rewrite: either remove those tests from cmd, or move them to handler package test file.\n\nHmm. The simplest approach that keeps things green: Move the migrated-function tests into the handler package (create `internal/handler/*_test.go`), and remove/adjust the references in cmd tests.\n\nBut wait — some tests in cmd still need to exist for cmd-specific behavior (like NewDoingCmd, NewPlanCmd). Let me categorize.\n\nActually, let me be strategic. The task's success criteria:\n1. `go build -o bin/rick ./cmd/rick` succeeds\n2. `go test ./internal/cmd/... ./internal/handler/... -timeout 60s -v` all green\n\nThe tests in cmd package that reference migrated functions will