{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The remaining dirty files are all pre-existing (they were dirty before I started, from other tasks / the job's own working files). My task6 changes are committed. The `.rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tasks.json` is now committed (no longer in status). Good.\n\nNote: `bin/rick` still shows `M` — it was already modified before, and I rebuilt it during testing. It's not part of my commit (consistent with prior task commits which didn't commit bin/rick). This is fine.\n\nThe task is complete:\n- ✅ Key Result 1: internal/handler package created with migrated functions\n- ✅ Key Result 2: cmd/{plan,doing,easy}.go thin, generateJobID deleted\n- ✅ Key Result 3: 8 commands unchanged\n- ✅ Key Result 4: doing still via executor, tests rewritten\n- ✅ Key Result 5: build + test green\n- ✅ doing_check passes\n\nLet me write a concise summary of the Loop execution.\n\nActually, wait — let me double-check one thing. The task's KR1 mentions handler orchestration should persist sessionID. In the current Easy/StartEasySession, sessionID is persisted via saveSessionID (to doing/session_id). That's already in handler. Plan and Doing don't persist sessionID (they use CallCLI interactive and executor respectively), which matches the \"本 task 中\" scope (runtime.Run sessionID return is task8). So this is aligned.\n\nLet me also verify I haven't broken the `easy` command's `--job` resume via the doing cmd. In doing.go cmd, the easy mode uses `if jobID == \"\" { jobID = GetJobID() }`. Then `handler.ResumeEasy(jobID, opts)`. That matches original behavior.\n\nOne more check: the `doing --easy --job <id>` resume path. Original easy.go had `--resume` flag for easy cmd, but doing cmd's easy mode used `--job`. Let me verify original doing.go: yes, in easy mode it did `if jobID == \"\" { jobID = GetJobID() }` then resumeEasyMode(jobID). I preserved that.\n\nEverything looks good. Let me provide the final summ